{
  "id": "interval-searches",
  "goals": [
    "Encl H E P for an evaluator E that a search calls, and the search's result for every such E",
    "RadiusIn P q lo hi: existence, uniqueness, and containment of a root between two certified points",
    "the result of two bisections from a bracket, with probes that the enclosure cannot decide",
    "the covered part [0, t] of an adaptive march bounds the function from below",
    "every element of LeanExe.loop cells.size.toUInt64 #[] fun i acc => step cells[i.toNat]! acc has a property, and a cell that holds a point leaves one that holds it",
    "cells.size.toUInt64.toNat = cells.size and a cap on the cells of a level",
    "an enclosure of the root of g x = 0 from a residual and a lower bound of the slope",
    "a branch-and-prune search over geodetic boxes that splits boxes near a pole",
    "a theorem of a search for every function within the margins that it tests",
    "an accepted panel lies within an accuracy of the least midpoint bound of the searches of the same kind",
    "an enclosure of an integral by a march whose panels have about equal widths, without an array",
    "the tolerance of a march for a budget of panels, from the widths of an earlier march",
    "a queue of cells in an append-only array under a budget of splits, with intervals inherited from the parent",
    "a witness of a value at or above a threshold from an interval at a cell center",
    "the number of panels that a fuel-bounded search evaluates",
    "a comparison of searches by the least panel count with status 0"
  ],
